  "id": "prepotent-response",
  "term": "prepotent response",
  "definition": "A prepotent response is the dominant response tendency that is most readily selected in a given situation. In tasks that test inhibition, it is the usual response that must be suppressed in order to make an alternative, non-dominant response.",
